 ## How It Was Delivered
 
-[How was this tested, verified and shipped? What was the rollout approach?]
+Seven steps. The hub skeleton was authored from the scaffolder's own assets and the sk-doc parent-skill templates, because `/create:skill-parent` hard-blocks without an `@markdown` persona that a non-interactive orchestrator session cannot adopt. The move was `mkdir -p` plus `git mv`, since `git mv` will not create the destination's parent. The retag rewrote the packet frontmatter, the registry row and the axis in one pass. The leaf manifest was regenerated from the new location. Then the identity pass classified every `cli-jev` occurrence in the packet by role: hub id, alias and dispatch display name stayed; packet name, titles and folder references moved to `cli-usage`. The hub's own playbook and benchmark were authored last, so their citations point at files that exist. Finally two read-only reviewers re-derived the phase's claims from the tree, and their findings were triaged before the closing gate run.
 <!-- /ANCHOR:how-delivered -->
 
